WEBVTT

00:07.530 --> 00:09.150
This is strange.

00:10.950 --> 00:14.420
It's the noon hour, 
but the bell hasn't rung.

00:14.420 --> 00:15.700
You're right.

00:15.700 --> 00:18.810
Ringing the bell to signify the hour
 is required by law.

00:18.810 --> 00:23.230
I know there's a state of emergency,
but I'm sure they could still manage that.

00:23.230 --> 00:24.670
My lady.

00:25.450 --> 00:29.630
I have a feeling this town 
is hiding something.

00:29.630 --> 00:32.130
Hiding something? Like what?

00:32.130 --> 00:35.090
Right now, all I'm really going
 off of is a hunch.

00:35.090 --> 00:39.420
<i>Well... Healran's instincts </i>have<i>
helped him uncover corruption.</i>

00:39.420 --> 00:41.050
So you want to look into this?

00:41.540 --> 00:42.700
Yes!

00:42.700 --> 00:44.030
<i>Now I'm kinda worried...</i>

00:44.360 --> 00:46.540
I'll leave whatever's afoot in town to you.

00:46.540 --> 00:48.210
But don't do anything rash.

00:48.210 --> 00:51.550
If anything happens, 
just flash the Osphe family crest.

00:51.550 --> 00:52.740
Understood.

00:52.970 --> 00:57.390
<i>I'll ask Lars to leave some 
wind spirits with him.</i>

00:57.390 --> 00:59.460
<i>Then, in the case of emergency...</i>

00:59.830 --> 01:02.670
<i>Lars will be able to alert Will.</i>

01:03.380 --> 01:08.860
<i>After that, we split up with Healran 
and checked out the city.</i>

01:09.640 --> 01:13.760
<i>In order to get the kobold 
pup we saved back home</i>

01:13.760 --> 01:18.190
<i>and in order to negotiate with the kobolds 
regarding Project Shiana,</i>

01:18.770 --> 01:24.050
<i>we headed into the forest 
to look for their hideout...</i>

01:24.430 --> 01:28.380
But no one told me it'd be this hard!

01:37.780 --> 01:42.700
<b><i>Fluffy Paradise</i></b>

02:59.530 --> 03:04.490
<b><i>Episode 9   Guardian of the Forest, Please...!</i></b>

03:01.360 --> 03:04.690
Hey... is it really this way?

03:06.140 --> 03:09.580
It feels like any visible path 
is just getting more and more...

03:11.940 --> 03:15.790
You two must be having fun. 
I guess monsters really do get along.

03:17.310 --> 03:19.040
"Hurry, hurry"?

03:19.040 --> 03:20.340
Hold your horses!

03:20.340 --> 03:23.380
<i>It's hard to really go that fast as a human child!</i>

03:24.310 --> 03:25.870
Shinki!

03:25.870 --> 03:27.960
Now you won't have to worry about tripping.

03:29.070 --> 03:30.840
Yeah, thanks!

03:35.070 --> 03:36.490
What's the matter?

03:36.830 --> 03:38.270
Is something there?!

03:38.270 --> 03:39.410
Is it a kobold?

03:44.200 --> 03:46.770
Wait... What is that?!

03:52.070 --> 03:54.480
It's... a slime.

03:54.480 --> 03:56.810
A-A slime?!

03:58.510 --> 04:01.270
<i>A super famous monster just appeared!</i>

04:01.270 --> 04:03.170
<i>It doesn't look like the game kind,</i>

04:03.480 --> 04:07.180
<i>but its still got that super squishy body!</i>

04:08.230 --> 04:10.630
I wonder what it feels like.

04:10.630 --> 04:14.140
Man, I really wanna squeeze it.

04:15.610 --> 04:16.780
What?

04:16.780 --> 04:19.080
It's asking for help.

04:19.080 --> 04:20.890
Shinki, you can understand it?

04:20.890 --> 04:21.480
Yeah.

04:21.740 --> 04:25.280
It's saying that it has a weakened
comrade up ahead,

04:25.280 --> 04:27.440
and it would like our assistance.

04:27.810 --> 04:30.950
What? Its comrade is weakened?

04:31.440 --> 04:34.920
Um, Ralf, I...

04:35.880 --> 04:38.170
You can follow your heart, Neema.

04:38.170 --> 04:41.430
If things get ugly, we'll protect you.

04:41.710 --> 04:44.740
When did I get roped into this?

04:44.740 --> 04:47.940
Don't worry. I was talking 
about Lars, not you.

04:49.100 --> 04:51.470
Thanks! Now that that's settled...

04:51.470 --> 04:56.170
I don't know if I can help, 
but could you lead us to them?

04:59.030 --> 05:00.240
Shinki!

05:02.060 --> 05:03.790
Lady Nefertima!

05:04.480 --> 05:07.510
It's dangerous, so we'll go on ahead.

05:14.760 --> 05:17.070
What the heck is that thing?!

05:19.250 --> 05:20.600
It's huge.

05:20.600 --> 05:23.880
I believe it's a parent slime.

05:23.880 --> 05:25.390
This thing?

05:25.390 --> 05:26.270
Yes.

05:26.630 --> 05:28.930
This is my first time seeing one as well,

05:28.930 --> 05:32.910
since slimes usually only 
show up in warm regions.

05:32.910 --> 05:36.980
Large slimes can produce countless tiny ones,

05:36.980 --> 05:39.890
which is why they're
 called parent slimes, I believe.

05:39.890 --> 05:44.060
Meaning those colorful 
things are all baby slimes?

05:44.060 --> 05:46.440
If all of them are born at once...

05:50.680 --> 05:52.560
Oh no! Here they come!

05:53.070 --> 05:55.750
W-Wait! Not here!

05:56.060 --> 05:58.180
It's cold and dangerous here,

05:58.180 --> 06:00.580
so wait until you're somewhere safe!

06:01.600 --> 06:03.600
I don't think it can move.

06:03.600 --> 06:05.310
So it'll give birth any minute?

06:05.310 --> 06:06.670
And that's not all.

06:07.190 --> 06:09.620
Once slimes become parent slimes,
they turn parasitic,

06:09.620 --> 06:11.880
completely unable to move on their own.

06:12.210 --> 06:15.630
But one this big would just 
get in the way if we carry it around.

06:16.370 --> 06:18.000
What should we do?

06:18.000 --> 06:22.610
If I remember correctly, they won't 
reproduce when inhabiting someone.

06:22.610 --> 06:24.310
Inhabiting someone?!

06:24.760 --> 06:25.770
Yeah.

06:25.770 --> 06:29.740
But... won't you get eaten
by the slime if that happens?

06:31.230 --> 06:33.320
It says it won't eat you if it likes you.

06:33.320 --> 06:36.150
Meaning it <i>will</i> eat you
if it doesn't like you!

06:36.440 --> 06:39.630
Out of curiosity,
 which of us would you <i>not</i> eat?

06:41.130 --> 06:42.820
It says you, my lady.

06:42.820 --> 06:44.500
<i>Go figure...</i>

06:44.500 --> 06:46.530
What about Shinki?

06:46.530 --> 06:49.480
<i>He's hot and has the best bod
 out of everyone here.</i>

06:50.980 --> 06:53.120
<i>Yeah, I saw that coming.</i>

06:54.790 --> 06:55.770
Hmm...

06:55.770 --> 07:00.590
Apparently once it inhabits you, 
anything you consume is eaten by the slime,

07:00.590 --> 07:03.010
so you won't have to go to the bathroom.

07:03.010 --> 07:04.430
<i>Say what?!</i>

07:04.810 --> 07:07.970
<i>In other words, 
all the nutrients go to the slime,</i>

07:07.970 --> 07:11.330
<i>so I can eat a bunch and 
not gain any weight?!</i>

07:11.330 --> 07:12.900
<i>That's great!</i>

07:13.740 --> 07:15.620
There you go, plotting again.

07:16.810 --> 07:19.870
It's saying that it'll protect you, my lady.

07:20.380 --> 07:22.660
Then maybe this is perfect.

07:22.660 --> 07:26.600
Due to the slime's nature, most physical 
attacks will be ineffective against you.

07:26.600 --> 07:29.360
Depending on the attribute, 
magic won't work either.

07:29.360 --> 07:32.390
I'd rather nothing inhabit Neema,
 but I guess we can

07:32.390 --> 07:34.710
play along if it's going to protect her.

07:35.000 --> 07:39.310
<i>True! We can get slimes involved 
in Project Shiana, too.</i>

07:39.820 --> 07:41.720
But are you really sure?

07:41.720 --> 07:45.330
Inhabiting me could mean
 a lot of trouble for you.

07:46.810 --> 07:48.980
All right, slime.

07:48.980 --> 07:51.980
My name is Nefertima Osphe.

07:52.270 --> 07:54.200
And your name will be...

07:54.630 --> 07:57.510
Shizuku. It's Shizuku!

07:57.930 --> 07:59.410
It's nice to meet you!

08:10.550 --> 08:14.910
Wow! It feels like a soft boob.

08:18.010 --> 08:19.270
This is so healing!

08:19.270 --> 08:20.120
Neema!

08:30.500 --> 08:32.180
I swallowed it...

08:32.180 --> 08:33.530
Neema, are you okay?!

08:34.630 --> 08:38.960
Yeah. I do feel Shizuku's 
consciousness, though.

08:38.960 --> 08:40.940
So this is what being inhabited is like...

08:43.170 --> 08:45.080
What are we going to do with that thing?

08:46.290 --> 08:51.170
Shizuku says that this one is going 
to be the next parent slime.

08:51.900 --> 08:54.420
Then we'll have to take it with us.

08:54.420 --> 08:55.570
Yeah.

08:56.020 --> 09:00.590
Let's find a safe place where you 
can have your babies together.

09:01.680 --> 09:03.600
You'll be... Let's see.

09:03.600 --> 09:04.920
Since you're all white...

09:05.340 --> 09:06.370
Haku.

09:07.170 --> 09:08.870
Yup, your name is Haku!

09:16.310 --> 09:19.580
Haku! Let me pet you!

09:21.470 --> 09:22.190
Huh?

09:22.530 --> 09:25.290
Ah, so this is a slime, huh?

09:26.680 --> 09:28.610
<i>Brute Prince!</i>

09:28.610 --> 09:32.210
<i>I guess there's something appealing 
about that texture to boys.</i>

09:32.900 --> 09:35.370
Pardon me, my lady.

09:36.870 --> 09:40.390
We should probably get going soon,
 or the kobold...

09:42.550 --> 09:46.150
Oh, sorry! I didn't forget about you.

09:46.150 --> 09:47.520
He's right.

09:48.250 --> 09:51.230
We need to go back 
to finding the kobolds first.

09:52.130 --> 09:54.030
Okay, let's go!

09:54.370 --> 09:55.610
Yeah!

10:02.340 --> 10:05.340
Hey, doesn't something seem strange?

10:06.890 --> 10:08.290
True.

10:08.590 --> 10:12.250
We've walked for quite a while, 
but the scenery hasn't changed.

10:12.540 --> 10:15.080
I don't sense any magic, though.

10:16.670 --> 10:18.940
The kobold pup is sad, too.

10:19.210 --> 10:21.260
Lars, do you sense anything?

10:24.370 --> 10:27.150
"Magic isn't the only phenomena,

10:27.150 --> 10:30.040
nor are living creatures 
and spirits everything.

10:30.040 --> 10:34.410
The God of Divine Creation's power overflows
 throughout the world," he says.

10:34.800 --> 10:36.560
Wow, Lars!

10:38.150 --> 10:40.460
<i>But I wonder what all that means.</i>

10:40.460 --> 10:43.530
<i>Is he's saying there's 
something besides magic?</i>

10:43.530 --> 10:46.990
<i>Perhaps there's something we 
haven't encountered before...</i>

10:48.110 --> 10:50.040
Hey, could it be...

10:54.810 --> 10:57.040
Neema, did you figure something out?

10:57.040 --> 10:59.640
The spirits are acting differently.

11:00.040 --> 11:05.240
Yes. I'm not certain yet, 
but it might be in this forest.

11:05.240 --> 11:07.680
For now, let's follow Lars.

11:08.850 --> 11:13.390
Shinki, you're not a monster from here, 
so I need you to wait for a second.

11:13.390 --> 11:16.620
Sorry, Gratia. You too. I'll be right back!

11:16.620 --> 11:17.360
Neema.

11:18.470 --> 11:22.600
It's probably not a human, spirit, 
or monster... But it's <i>something</i>.

11:23.090 --> 11:26.270
There was something about it 
in that book you read to me, Will.

11:26.560 --> 11:28.110
I'm surprised you remember.

11:28.110 --> 11:31.590
Is that the reason 
we've been going around in circles?

11:32.020 --> 11:34.290
If it's what I think it is,

11:34.290 --> 11:37.410
it might know something 
about the kobolds, too.

11:37.710 --> 11:41.820
<i>Yes. Deep, deep in the forest,</i>

11:42.400 --> 11:45.880
<i>there's a sanctuary where only 
those granted permission may enter.</i>

11:50.120 --> 11:51.890
<i>It's really here!</i>

11:55.720 --> 11:59.600
<i>There are times when certain rare 
creatures that live a long time</i>

11:59.600 --> 12:03.930
<i>evolve into something that will protect 
a territory with special powers.</i>

12:03.930 --> 12:06.710
<i>These beings are called guardians.</i>

12:10.430 --> 12:14.150
So this is the guardian of this forest!

12:14.150 --> 12:17.670
A being that isn't magical,
nor is it a living creature or a spirit.

12:20.370 --> 12:22.770
I wonder if I can approach it.

12:24.370 --> 12:25.800
Be careful.

12:28.260 --> 12:30.510
Thanks, Ralf.

12:31.060 --> 12:33.700
<i>Thank you for always letting me do what I want.</i>

12:33.700 --> 12:36.510
<i>I truly appreciate you, Ralf.</i>

12:37.280 --> 12:38.600
Go on, Neema.

12:49.100 --> 12:52.030
It's a pleasure to meet you,
 Guardian of the Forest.

12:52.030 --> 12:54.290
My name is Nefertima Osphe.

12:54.610 --> 12:58.250
I apologize for all the trouble we've caused.

13:00.060 --> 13:05.680
You needn't apologize, Nefertima Osphe.

13:07.280 --> 13:10.840
But what a peculiar group you all are.

13:11.120 --> 13:16.480
You have a holy beast, a child of 
royalty, and even some monsters.

13:16.480 --> 13:18.810
Just who are you, little girl?

13:19.060 --> 13:23.780
<i>Who am I? I can't just say 
that I'm helping out God...</i>

13:24.090 --> 13:30.250
Um... My father holds our family title,
so you can just call me Nefertima.

13:32.020 --> 13:34.260
What a strange child.

13:34.260 --> 13:37.660
So, what did you need from me?

13:39.650 --> 13:41.020
Well...

13:42.160 --> 13:45.090
We're actually looking 
for this little one's mother.

13:45.090 --> 13:48.110
Do you know where the kobolds' hideout is?

13:48.390 --> 13:51.060
What will you do once you find it?

13:51.060 --> 13:54.230
I want to see this little 
one back to his mother.

13:54.230 --> 13:55.930
Even though he's a monster?

13:55.930 --> 13:58.970
That doesn't matter. I just 
want to see him home because...

13:59.270 --> 14:01.940
he's clearly in distress.

14:03.650 --> 14:05.820
I see.

14:05.820 --> 14:10.990
But I'm sorry, little girl. 
I cannot disclose that information.

14:11.330 --> 14:12.700
Why is that?

14:12.960 --> 14:18.760
Humans persistently pursued the kobolds
until they were driven into these woods.

14:18.760 --> 14:22.500
It was truly a terrible sight.

14:22.500 --> 14:27.380
I pitied them, so I decided 
to hide them from the humans.

14:27.720 --> 14:32.410
Guardian of the Forest, I know what
 the humans did to them was awful.

14:32.410 --> 14:34.140
I'm very sorry!

14:34.140 --> 14:39.710
But we just want to see this little one back 
to his mother and negotiate with the kobolds!

14:40.430 --> 14:41.560
Negotiate?

14:41.870 --> 14:42.680
Yes.

14:43.300 --> 14:48.000
We're thinking about having them 
move to a different location.

14:48.000 --> 14:52.660
The proxy lord of Lenice is planning 
to send an extermination squad here.

14:52.660 --> 14:54.920
If you keep hiding them,

14:54.920 --> 14:59.690
it will put you and the other 
animals in this forest in danger.

15:00.690 --> 15:03.160
The situation is already dire!

15:03.160 --> 15:07.080
I don't think we can avoid a fight 
between the humans and kobolds.

15:07.360 --> 15:13.560
I see. I suppose I cannot 
keep them hidden forever.

15:13.910 --> 15:18.260
Getting them enough food is also an issue.

15:19.700 --> 15:20.900
Yes.

15:20.900 --> 15:23.550
I would like to do everything I can for them.

15:23.550 --> 15:27.220
I want to help the kobolds.
Guardian of the Forest...

15:27.990 --> 15:29.350
Please.

15:30.470 --> 15:33.900
Could you please guide me to their hideout?

15:34.720 --> 15:38.600
Very well. I shall trust in you, little girl.

15:38.600 --> 15:42.790
But should I ever find out
you've deceived me,

15:42.790 --> 15:45.880
you will not leave this forest alive.

15:49.090 --> 15:52.110
I may not be able to save them all...

15:52.110 --> 15:55.290
But if you can accept that,
I will swear upon my name!

15:57.340 --> 16:00.480
No, you needn't go so far.

16:00.480 --> 16:03.380
Once things are put into motion,

16:03.380 --> 16:08.340
the God of Divine Creation will 
decide how they proceed.

16:14.190 --> 16:16.460
Now go.

16:16.750 --> 16:19.920
Guardian of the Forest... Thank you!

16:20.340 --> 16:22.950
The spirits will guide you.

16:22.950 --> 16:25.910
Once all is said and done, 
come see me again sometime.

16:25.910 --> 16:26.760
I will!

16:27.790 --> 16:29.840
Isn't that great? Let's go.

16:35.350 --> 16:38.020
Progress has certainly gotten easier.

16:38.020 --> 16:40.270
Well, we have the guardian 
of the forest's blessing.

16:40.710 --> 16:42.100
Hmm...

16:42.100 --> 16:42.970
What's the matter?

16:43.240 --> 16:45.930
Well, the guardian of the 
forest mentioned this too,

16:45.930 --> 16:48.160
but getting the monsters enough food to eat

16:48.160 --> 16:50.460
will be a problem with Project Shiana, too.

16:50.460 --> 16:52.780
True, I guess we hadn't considered that.

16:52.780 --> 16:56.640
Say, what do goblins eat other than fruit?

16:56.640 --> 16:58.190
We'll eat anything.

16:58.190 --> 17:00.110
What about kobolds?

17:00.370 --> 17:02.830
Um, I think they're omnivores.

17:03.140 --> 17:04.970
Omnivores?

17:04.970 --> 17:08.290
<i>I guess we'll probably have to grow crops...</i>

17:10.260 --> 17:11.750
What's wrong?

17:13.800 --> 17:15.290
You too, Nox?

17:23.350 --> 17:25.970
Huh?! A b-bug?!

17:25.970 --> 17:29.500
That's a bug monster. It's called a mamushi.

17:29.500 --> 17:33.110
Some are poisonous, which is probably
why they were so on guard.

17:36.530 --> 17:37.980
Speaking of food...

17:38.250 --> 17:40.200
Those are edible.

17:40.200 --> 17:42.220
Say what now?!

17:42.220 --> 17:43.790
They're great roasted.

17:47.720 --> 17:49.830
That's impressive.

17:52.000 --> 17:55.570
You get this big piece, Lars. 
And you get this one.

17:55.570 --> 17:56.250
My lady.

17:58.220 --> 17:59.440
Would you like some?

17:59.440 --> 18:01.310
You don't have to force yourself, Neema.

18:01.310 --> 18:02.820
I-I'll be fine...

18:02.820 --> 18:05.880
<i>I've got Shizuku, so it shouldn't 
upset my stomach.</i>

18:11.420 --> 18:13.100
<i>I-It's good!</i>

18:13.520 --> 18:18.070
<i>Why does it have the texture 
of lobster and taste like white fish?</i>

18:18.070 --> 18:21.270
<i>This would be superb with some booze!</i>

18:21.710 --> 18:24.180
You can have some too, Gratia.

18:26.460 --> 18:29.220
Can't knock it till you've tried it.
Here goes.

18:29.220 --> 18:30.880
Wait, Will, are you ser—

18:32.960 --> 18:34.370
It's not bad.

18:34.670 --> 18:38.080
It lacks flavor, but that can be 
remedied with the right preparation.

18:38.520 --> 18:40.100
Did you also want to try some?

18:42.520 --> 18:43.770
Do you like it?

18:44.080 --> 18:48.160
Yeah. The flavor's really light.
I think I can eat it as-is.

18:48.980 --> 18:51.480
It's good! It's really tasty!

18:51.480 --> 18:53.950
We can probably use its 
shell for something, too!

18:54.270 --> 18:58.520
Right. The adventurers' guild or the 
blacksmiths' guild will buy that from you.

18:58.830 --> 19:01.500
<i>Wow, how convenient!</i>

19:01.770 --> 19:06.280
Lars, if you see any more of those bugs, 
I'd like for you to hunt them down.

19:06.750 --> 19:09.190
You too, knights.

19:09.490 --> 19:14.920
Sure... I don't mind, but what are 
you going to do with all of them?

19:18.130 --> 19:21.430
I'm going to give them 
to the kobolds as a gift.

19:24.880 --> 19:29.720
<i>I have a feeling the mamushis will be 
super useful for Project Shiana.</i>

19:30.030 --> 19:32.200
What a haul!

19:32.490 --> 19:34.710
We've gotten pretty deep into the forest.

19:34.710 --> 19:37.160
Can we make it back 
to the city before evening?

19:37.390 --> 19:40.100
The spirits seem to be leading us this way.

19:43.010 --> 19:44.990
Huh? What? What is it?

19:45.320 --> 19:46.980
There's nothing there.

19:47.370 --> 19:49.470
No, that's not true.

19:49.470 --> 19:50.120
Huh?

19:57.800 --> 19:58.700
They're here!

19:59.010 --> 20:03.820
Um, we've come with the 
guardian of the forest's blessing!

20:03.820 --> 20:07.180
We came to see your leader!

20:10.070 --> 20:12.640
They're saying they can't trust us.

20:12.640 --> 20:14.260
<i>Of course not...</i>

20:14.690 --> 20:17.940
Um, we've brought you a gift!

20:17.940 --> 20:20.720
Delicious mamushi meat!

20:21.000 --> 20:22.580
If you'd like some...

20:25.120 --> 20:28.730
They said they're going to talk 
to their leader, so follow them.

20:28.730 --> 20:31.140
Okay, let's go.

20:45.490 --> 20:48.970
<i>Th-This is heaven!</i>

20:49.300 --> 20:51.540
<i>This is truly fluffy heaven!</i>

20:51.540 --> 20:53.200
<i>I want to take them all home with me!</i>

20:53.200 --> 20:54.030
My lady?

20:54.030 --> 20:57.100
<i>Now I really need to bring them into my plan!</i>

20:57.100 --> 21:01.240
Oh, I'm sorry. Let's find your mommy first.

21:04.250 --> 21:05.610
Human child!

21:06.640 --> 21:08.930
What do you want with us?

21:08.930 --> 21:12.700
Wow, she's so pretty!

21:13.450 --> 21:15.550
Oh, sorry.

21:15.880 --> 21:19.520
It's a pleasure to meet you. 
My name is Nefertima Osphe.

21:19.520 --> 21:23.270
We came to return this little 
one we saved in Lenice.

21:23.530 --> 21:26.470
He does indeed belong to our pack.

21:26.800 --> 21:28.790
Why did you go to the city?

21:30.850 --> 21:32.230
What?!

21:32.510 --> 21:35.700
You little runts! How dare you lie to me?!

21:35.700 --> 21:36.970
Huh? What?

21:36.970 --> 21:39.700
Apparently some other pups left him behind.

21:40.560 --> 21:42.970
Now, now! Please calm down, ma'am!

21:42.970 --> 21:43.370
Huh?

21:44.070 --> 21:47.320
There's no point in getting so mad.

21:47.570 --> 21:52.280
We've brought you gifts. 
Why don't we eat first?

21:53.800 --> 21:56.800
<i>I need to smile so they'll trust me.</i>

21:56.800 --> 22:02.810
<i>And then once their tummies are full,
 it's negotiation time!</i>

22:03.330 --> 22:04.280
Tee-hee!

23:35.220 --> 23:40.050
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.220 --> 23:40.050
<b>Let's Have a Strategy Meeting!</b>
